<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>World | Deutsche Welle</title><subtitle type="html">World | Deutsche Welle</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-world</id><updated>2026-11-19T17:29:38Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-world" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/english/?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-world" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>EU Commission confirms it was targeted in cyberattack using AI tools</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3515dc70da031b9d958b40d0c686c1df9accf87c2fa5393233ea9cf1bdb88f0b</id><updated>2026-11-19T17:29:26Z</updated><published>2026-11-19T14:58:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/eu-commission-confirms-it-was-targeted-in-cyberattack-using-ai-tools/a-79993016--2e1cd85b257c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/eu-commission-confirms-it-was-targeted-in-cyberattack-using-ai-tools/a-79993016?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The European Commission was targeted by an "AI-generated cybercampaign," a spokesperson has said. This is the first time the bloc has publicly reported an AI-based cyberattack.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Wadephul: 'Coalition of the Willing' talks in Berlin send strong signal to Moscow</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fb093409afd832188b2fd345a80ec29eb66d5c702d11a9a61998ffc743e42ea0</id><updated>2026-11-19T17:29:29Z</updated><published>2026-11-19T13:56:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/wadephul-coalition-of-the-willing-talks-in-berlin-send-strong-signal-to-moscow/a-79990664--ce1ce93ebd6c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/wadephul-coalition-of-the-willing-talks-in-berlin-send-strong-signal-to-moscow/a-79990664?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">German Foreign Minister Wadephul has said the Coalition of the Willing meeting in Berlin sends a clear message to Moscow to take peace talks seriously. He also warned Ukraine should be prepared for peace talks to fail.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Pakistan minister to visit India, but no breakthrough expected</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:34fdd47cf7bca88150ad4962afe32d7905a0b2e389c76877ca38819dc0f0c55e</id><updated>2026-11-19T17:29:32Z</updated><published>2026-11-19T13:26:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/pakistan-minister-to-visit-india-but-no-breakthrough-expected/a-79991717--07503556e8b2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/pakistan-minister-to-visit-india-but-no-breakthrough-expected/a-79991717?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A Pakistani minister's visit to India for a Shanghai Cooperation Organization forum marks a rare high-level contact between the two archrivals, but analysts say it does not signal a resumption of bilateral engagement.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Myanmar committed genocide against Rohingya, top UN court rules</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f4044d7da9a755147b2376f563a7dc702bf6f587da7066a1845428b585b0d75c</id><updated>2026-11-19T17:29:38Z</updated><published>2026-11-19T11:39:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/myanmar-committed-genocide-against-rohingya-top-un-court-rules/a-79987898--1622af9cbda3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/myanmar-committed-genocide-against-rohingya-top-un-court-rules/a-79987898?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The International Court of Justice has upheld large parts of a genocide case against Myanmar linked to the 2017 conflict with its Rohingya minority. It called for it to pay reparations and let refugees return safely.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Is the AI bubble bursting just as Anthropic goes public?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:953002283f1a057bcdaf65f5475b1865d11da2ab95d436bac3cc592186de2106</id><updated>2026-11-19T17:28:25Z</updated><published>2026-11-19T05:58:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/is-the-ai-bubble-bursting-just-as-anthropic-goes-public/a-79896537--10f78cdc2264.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/is-the-ai-bubble-bursting-just-as-anthropic-goes-public/a-79896537?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The sharp sell-off in tech stocks after the US midterms and the Nvidia scandal has cast doubt on Anthropic's IPO. Yet with hundreds of billions still being invested, some think the AI party is still in full swing.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Almost 1 in 4 children live in conflict zones — report</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c23daff1d7a561fbb06c2980c2b5d9829bd1036398c3ccce55c422cc8c98f0a2</id><updated>2026-11-19T17:28:25Z</updated><published>2026-11-19T00:34:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/almost-1-in-4-children-live-in-conflict-zones-report/a-79979203--07598193af0c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/almost-1-in-4-children-live-in-conflict-zones-report/a-79979203?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Denial of humanitarian access, abductions and sexual violence are among several violations against children that have increased dramtically over the past year, according to a new report by Save the Children.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>North Korea expanded uranium enrichment plant, says IAEA head</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b6843ee026f02e5266b6270f1386bdf980a92f2f08a46eb6a5204a5a121544af</id><updated>2026-11-19T17:28:25Z</updated><published>2026-11-18T15:15:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/north-korea-expanded-uranium-enrichment-plant-says-iaea-head/a-79982758--65619f1023d6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/north-korea-expanded-uranium-enrichment-plant-says-iaea-head/a-79982758?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">IAEA chief Rafael Grossi has said the ongoing expansion of North Korea's uranium enrichment program remains "a cause for serious concern."</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>India: Online censorship grows after 'Cockroach' protests</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f527c9114dcf8efd0e17cb9601930a447087f5fdd655c6dedc7f67c0c39d3a23</id><updated>2026-11-19T17:28:25Z</updated><published>2026-11-18T14:28:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-online-censorship-grows-after-cockroach-protests/a-79976982--a74d2015326f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-online-censorship-grows-after-cockroach-protests/a-79976982?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Since anti-government Cockroach protests erupted, journalists and creators say their content is increasingly being restricted on social media in India.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>ICJ to rule on Rohingya genocide case against Myanmar: What to know</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0879868e2928a24ca96cf28095928fb5828ebdcc531c5111c18f872b91f09dc0</id><updated>2026-11-19T17:28:25Z</updated><published>2026-11-18T14:27:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/icj-to-rule-on-rohingya-genocide-case-against-myanmar-what-to-know/a-79981434--76de3c2375bc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/icj-to-rule-on-rohingya-genocide-case-against-myanmar-what-to-know/a-79981434?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The ICJ is set to decide whether Myanmar's military operations in Rakhine State a decade ago were carried out with the intent to destroy the country's Rohingya minority, in whole or in part.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Axes and cutlasses: Violence on Nigeria's election campaign trail</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e578965c6a08b4d0f2e8d29938adad720a7a02bff3d0e1bd0b5cca25c76aba7f</id><updated>2026-11-19T17:28:25Z</updated><published>2026-11-18T10:56:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/axes-and-cutlasses-violence-on-nigeria-s-election-campaign-trail/a-79978467--351fdc554734.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/axes-and-cutlasses-violence-on-nigeria-s-election-campaign-trail/a-79978467?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As Nigeria's January 2027 elections approach, political violence and thuggery at campaign rallies and town hall meetings raise concerns about voter safety.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Latin America's mega-prisons: Can El Salvador's model work?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3d3f59f1928bb63e70a5bc9d6990f5e9dd5741a363040e05519f3c45a28aa244</id><updated>2026-11-19T17:28:25Z</updated><published>2026-11-18T10:45:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/latin-america-s-mega-prisons-can-el-salvador-s-model-work/a-79973524--e4fa38fb46de.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/latin-america-s-mega-prisons-can-el-salvador-s-model-work/a-79973524?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">El Salvador's mega-prison has become a model for governments across Latin America seeking to combat organized crime. But experts question whether the approach is effective, sustainable or compatible with human rights.</summary><category term="World" /></entry></feed>
